  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asian Elephant Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to achieve conservation of the Northern Karnataka elephant population through mitigation of human-elephant conflict (HEC) and knowledge-based conservation planning. By reducing crop damage in the project area applicant hopes to raise the tolerance of farmers to elephant presence and contribute to conservation of elephants. HEC is expected to increase in coming years given that many farmers in the project area are taking up sugarcane cultivation. Applicant will carry out experiments on low cost elephant deterrent measures and implement them with the involvement of local people. Objectives include, (1) implementation of Community-based Conflict Management (CBCM) in affected villages with involvement of local farmers and capacity building of the farmers in implementation of these measures, (2) carrying out experiments to assess the effectiveness of low-cost mitigation measures on captive elephants, (3) creating a database of wild elephants in the project area by building visual identification key for each elephant, (4) mapping and assessing quality of habitat for elephants and identification and assessment of corridors in Belgaum Division, (5) extension programs for creating awareness on CBCM model and elephant conservation.</narrative>
  </description>
